script:post-response {
  // Get the 'X-Entity-Id' header from the response
  let person2Id = res.headers["x-entity-id"];
  
  // If the header exists, store it as an environment variable
  if (person2Id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("person2Id", person2Id);
  }
  
}

tests {
  // postman.setGlobalVariable("person2Id", res.getHeader("X-Entity-Id"));
  
}

docs {
  The /tree/persons endpoint creates a new person record based on the information provided in the Request Body. The request body specifies the Tree Id of the new user tree created in Step (1-4).
  
  This request in the collection persists the Person Id as person2Id in the global variables. This person ID will be used in the creation of relationships in Steps (4-1) and (4-2).
  
  If the status code from this request is 201 Created, proceed to (2-3) Add Person.
}
